%% Deletion protection on Contoso account - which delete is reversible, for how long, and what the reversal does NOT bring back
%% Source: Microsoft Learn - Azure file share soft delete (retention 1 to 365 days, default 7, undelete restores snapshots, permanent delete needs undelete then disable then delete); Recover a deleted storage account (14 days, best effort, resource group must exist, linked private endpoints are removed and not recreated); codex/runbook-restore-file-share-and-share-soft-delete.md classes 4 and 5; codex/blueprint-azure-files-secure-storage-account.md step 6
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR

  state "One file share - home-drives, dept-shares or archive" as SHARE {
    direction TB
    state "Active. Soft delete is on at the ACCOUNT level, so the setting covers every share in stmryfiles01 at once" as ACTIVE
    state "Leased by Azure Backup. While the share is protected, an infinite snapshot lease means a delete is no longer one click" as LEASED
    state "Soft deleted. Listed by az storage share-rm list --include-deleted with a remainingRetentionDays counter and a deleted-version id" as SOFT
    state "Undeleted. The share AND all of its snapshots come back in their pre-deletion state, and the File Sync cloud endpoint resumes" as UNDEL
    state "Permanently gone. Retention elapsed, or an operator ran the deliberate three-step - undelete the share, disable soft delete, delete it again" as GONE

    [*] --> ACTIVE
    ACTIVE --> LEASED : protected by the vault
    ACTIVE --> SOFT : deleted
    LEASED --> SOFT : deleted after the lease is broken
    SOFT --> UNDEL : az storage share-rm restore with the deleted-version, inside the window
    UNDEL --> ACTIVE
    SOFT --> GONE : remainingRetentionDays reaches zero
    UNDEL --> GONE : the deliberate purge path, three steps, never accidental
  }

  state "The storage account stmryfiles01" as ACCOUNT {
    direction TB
    state "Live with a CanNotDelete lock. The lock is the ONLY control here that is preventive rather than compensating" as LOCKED
    state "Live with no lock. Assessor SEC-09" as UNLOCKED
    state "Deleted. A restore is possible for 14 days, is BEST EFFORT and is not guaranteed" as DELETED
    state "Restored. Requires the original resource group to still exist, no new account of the same name, and Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/write on the caller" as RESTORED
    state "Unrecoverable. Past 14 days, or the resource group was deleted too - a resource group cannot be recovered at all" as LOST

    [*] --> UNLOCKED
    UNLOCKED --> LOCKED : az lock create -t CanNotDelete
    LOCKED --> UNLOCKED : an operator with lock write removes it, which is the real attack path
    UNLOCKED --> DELETED : one portal click
    DELETED --> RESTORED : portal Restore, inside 14 days
    DELETED --> LOST : window elapsed or the resource group went with it
    RESTORED --> UNLOCKED
  }

  note right of ACCOUNT
    What a successful account restore does NOT bring back.
    Every linked private endpoint is removed with the account
    and is not recreated by the restore, so Contoso must
    re-create the file endpoint, re-approve the connection and
    re-point the privatelink.file.core.windows.net A record
    before a single server can mount again. If the account
    used a customer-managed key and the key vault was deleted
    as well, the vault has to be restored FIRST.
  end note

  note left of SHARE
    Three different windows, three different owners, and only
    the first two are share-level. Share soft delete is 1 to 365
    days and defaults to 7 - Contoso sets 14 because Azure
    Backup requires at least 14. Backup snapshot retention runs
    on the policy. Vault-tier retention runs on Contoso
    records schedule. Soft delete recovers a deleted SHARE,
    never a deleted file inside a live share - that is a
    snapshot or a backup restore.
  end note
